<title>USA: U.S. June durable goods orders rose 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. June durable goods orders rose 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent</p>
<p>changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:     June     May--Rev from     Apr</p>
<p>  New Orders		  2.3    -0.4    -0.7	 1.8</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.   7.5    -0.9    -3.0	 2.8</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.     0.8    -0.2     0.2	 1.5</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	 2.1     0.1    -0.3	 1.1</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders	9.9   -12.0   -13.0	27.5</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders   5.4     1.1     0.4	-1.7</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts    1.7    -0.5     0.3	-1.5</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:   June	May---Rev from     Apr</p>
<p> New Orders		180.58   176.48   175.86    177.11</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  42.30    39.35    38.52     39.72</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   138.28   137.13   137.68    137.40</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     174.51   170.96   170.40    170.84</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	6.07     5.52     5.46	6.27</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  46.64    44.24    43.92     43.75</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   39.04    38.37    38.69     38.57</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	June    May--Rev from     Apr</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    1.8    -1.5    -1.4	 1.3</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders    0.3     0.1     UNCH     -0.3</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:   June	May---Rev from     Apr</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 179.06   175.83   176.02    178.48</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   498.84   497.32   496.51    496.67</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   June    May--Rev from     Apr</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	    0.4    -2.4    -1.9	 2.4</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   -0.6    -3.1    -1.5	 3.0</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery    UNCH   10.7    10.0	-3.2</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  15.59    15.53   15.61     15.90</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  32.61    32.81   33.35     33.86</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  30.87    30.87   30.69     27.88</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected June durable goods orders to rise 1.4 percent.</p>
<p>The 2.3 percent rise in overall June durable goods orders was the largest since a 3.4 percent gain in January 1997, the department said.</p>
<p>Aircraft and parts orders accounted for more than half of the increase in transportation orders, it said.</p>
<p>Non-defense durables orders recorded their fifth increase in the last six months.</p>
</text>
